# Copyright & Takedown Policy

Zenthi is a platform for community-shared 3D-printable car part files. Every uploader confirms at submission that they created the file, or otherwise have the right to share it, and grants Zenthi a license to host and redistribute it.

## How this works

**Zenthi does not independently verify the ownership or authorship of every file.** With community-submitted content at scale, that isn't possible. The system relies on uploader attestation, admin review, and reports from rights holders.

If you believe a file on Zenthi infringes your copyright, or was uploaded without the proper rights, report it.

## Reporting a concern

**[→ Submit a copyright report](https://zenthi3d.lovable.app/copyright-policy)**

You'll be asked for:

| Field | What's needed |
| --- | --- |
| Your name | Full name |
| Your email | Where we'll follow up if we need more information |
| Part or file in question | The part name, or a link to the part listing |
| Description of the concern | What the file is, what right you hold, and why you believe it was shared without permission |

Submitting also requires confirming a good-faith belief that the use of the file is not authorised by the copyright owner, its agent, or the law, and that the information in the report is accurate.

## What happens next

- When a valid report is received, the file in question is **promptly removed or access-disabled** while the matter is reviewed.
- If more information is needed, you'll be contacted at the email address provided in the report.
- Contributors who repeatedly, or clearly, upload files they have no right to share may be **permanently removed** from contributing to the platform.

